# kirby-cost — optional test inputs.
#
# Copy to .env.test (untracked) and fill in the paths that exist on your
# machine. tests/conftest.py reads that file at import, so a full run is
# `pytest`, from a shell or an IDE runner alike. Anything already set in the
# environment wins, so a one-off override still works:
#
#     KIRBY_COST_CORPUS=/somewhere/else pytest tests/test_oracle_fixtures.py
#
# kirby-cost ships no Hero Games content — no templates, no character files,
# no oracle corpus. Every path below points into material you licensed and
# installed yourself, which is why none of them have defaults. Leave any of
# them out and the tests that need it skip; the suite passes either way
# (378 passed / 165 skipped with nothing set at all).
#
# Configure ALL of them and the skip guard arms: any skip then fails the run,
# because with nothing left to blame a skip means coverage went missing rather
# than "unrunnable here". See tests/corpus.py.

# A HERO Designer .hdt template. Costs are meaningless without one, so this is
# the variable that matters most — unset, roughly 900 tests skip.
# conftest.py also falls back to HERODesignerSource/template/Main6E.hdt if you
# keep an untracked copy in the repo, in which case leave this blank.
KIRBY_COST_HDT=~/HERODesigner/template/Main6E.hdt

# A directory of .hdc character packs, in whatever subdirectory layout you
# like. Tests reach into it by relative path.
KIRBY_COST_CORPUS=~/path/to/your/hdc-packs

# A HERO Designer document store — the folder HD saves into, holding the
# character packs you have purchased.
KIRBY_COST_HERO_DOCS=~/Documents/Champions

# The headless HERO Designer comparison CLI: a wrapper script that dumps HD's
# own costs as JSON, which is what the engine is compared against. It wraps
# licensed source and is not public, so this is maintainer-only.
KIRBY_COST_HD6CLI=~/path/to/hd6cli.sh

# One structurally awkward character, roundtripped whole against the oracle.
# Frameworks and containers are the point — a Multipower with slots, a
# CompoundPower, a maneuver or two. Nothing asserts WHICH character it is, so
# point this at any sufficiently gnarly .hdc of your own; there is no shared
# artifact to name and no default worth writing.
KIRBY_COST_ROUNDTRIP_HDC=~/path/to/a-complex-character.hdc
